# Notes — exp-backtest-1-muse check c1

- Fresh evidence (verify stance): `dune build` ok; `./test/harness.sh` -> "all checks passed" (exit 0); `backtest.json` loads: ok=true, tapes_replayed=2001, traces=2001, identifiable=1854, findings=720. Live `bp3 harness backtest` smoke: good/torn traces fold, missing corpus -> E_NOT_FOUND.
- Gated matrix rows verified: findings.md quotes (ungradeable note; `01a1ace8` E_DIR sample) present; ledger submit line on `bp3/exp/...` branch stamps run_id/harness/model at commit d7f0463; HEAD == bound commit, `git status --porcelain` empty; submit tape.log + notes.md present; `bp3 q r` folds to submitted/cycle 1/same commit (no hand-edited state).
- FAIL root cause: commit-sha extraction is dead. 0/2001 traces carry `commits` though the tapes contain 40-hex shas (e.g. `1576a8aa...`); synthetic pure-hex tapes also yield `commits: []`. `src/quest/harness.ml` `extract_shas` uses `Str.regexp "[0-9a-f]\\{40\\}"`; a standalone OCaml probe shows that pattern matches nothing (`string_match` = false) — Str has no `\{n\}` repetition, so it can only match literal `{40}` text. `test/harness.sh` never asserts the `commits` field, so the suite stays green while a rung-1 extraction ("git commits" per Run, demo commit-vs-ledger match) silently reports empty.
- Lesson: assert every extracted field at least once in fixtures (a known sha in the good tape would have caught this); an always-empty list is a misleading trace, not a legible finding.
- Unchecked: full `make check` (verdict already decided at rung 3); no whole-tape read (rung 5 not needed).
- Check-edge call outcome: refused `E_ILLEGAL_EDGE` — a parallel review child had already moved the exp `submitted -> blocked` (ledger 2026-11-15T23:55:43Z, verdict `needs_fix`) citing the same commits-extraction defect. Legal edges from `blocked` are only `resume`/`delete`, so this check verdict (fail, same root cause) could not be recorded without forcing state; it is reported in the reply JSON instead.

