# Notes — review exp-backtest-1-muse c1

- Verdict: needs_fix (code-reviewer fix_first). Rungs 1-3 decided it; no whole-tape (rung 5) read.
- Rung 1/2: HEAD == bound commit d7f0463, clean tree. Acceptance requires per-Run trace extracting git commits (TL;DR + Demo commit-vs-ledger match).
- Rung 3 defect (major): `extract_shas` never matches. Probe tape with two valid 40-hex shas -> `commits:[]`; submitted backtest.json: 0/2001 traces carry commits. `test/harness.sh` backtest section never asserts `.commits`, so the claim is untested. All other checks pass: harness.sh exit 0, backtest.json 2001/1854/720 corroborates findings.md, refusal/torn/foreign + E_NOT_FOUND/E_USAGE paths work.
- Minor: E_* extraction is noisy (pseudo-codes like E_QM2Q in approval-review tapes) — legibility cost only, findings-machine does not gate on it.
- Lesson: assert every extracted trace field in fixtures; an unasserted field can be silently empty across the whole corpus while counts stay green.

