Aliases: s=supervisor, i=init-check, f=find-tape, w=watch, d=desk, r=record-init, b=backtest. Example: bp3 harness supervisor toy --timeout-seconds 1800
bp3 harness backtest - replay the muse fold over stored tapes (findings, not a gate):
bp3 harness backtest [--corpus <dir>]
Reads every .jsonl tape under the corpus (default: the muse tape source), folds mechanical facts per tape (BP3_RUN_ID bindings, bp3 invocations, E_* refusals, commit shas, finish/exit evidence, torn tails) and emits one verdict {ok, engine, corpus, tapes_replayed, identifiable, traces, findings}. Each finding names its tape, run-id, evidence lines, and proposed fix target (bp3 q u, hooks, or adapter). A parser crash fails the call; findings themselves never gate. Truncated, foreign, and torn tapes are reported in findings, never fatal.
Example: bp3 harness backtest --corpus ~/.local/share/muse/sessions
